<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{.title}}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{.description}}">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{.url}}">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{.url}}">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{.title}}">
<meta property="og:description" content="{{.description}}">
<meta property="og:image" content="{{.socialImage.src}}">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{.socialImage.alt}}">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<link rel="preload" href="assets/fonts/tektur-var.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="assets/fonts/martian-mono-var.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<meta name="theme-color" content="#04070b">
<script>document.documentElement.classList.add("js")</script>
{{style "assets/styles/main.css"}}
</head>
<body>
<header class="top">
  <a class="brand" href="{{.urls.home}}">GhostPaw<span class="crumb">/questlog</span></a>
  <nav aria-label="questlog elsewhere">
    <a href="{{.urls.demo}}">Live demo</a>
    <a href="{{.urls.github}}">GitHub</a>
    <a href="{{.urls.npm}}">npm</a>
  </nav>
</header>
<main>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="kicker"><code>@ghostpaw/questlog</code> <span class="ver">0.9.1</span></p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Your agent said it was done. Was it?</h1>
      <p class="lede">An agent that ticks its own box gets to grade its own homework, so questlog makes it write the homework down: no quest is done without an outcome, and work that waits on other work stays blocked until that work is done.</p>
      <div class="install">
        <p class="cmd-label" id="lib-label">As a library</p>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="cmd-lib" readonly value="npm install @ghostpaw/questlog" aria-labelledby="lib-label" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="cmd-lib">Copy</button></div>
        <p class="cmd-label" id="mcp-label">As a local MCP server</p>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="cmd-mcp" readonly value="npx -y @ghostpaw/questlog mcp" aria-labelledby="mcp-label" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="cmd-mcp">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <p class="actions"><a class="button" href="#board">Try to finish a quest</a> <a href="{{.urls.github}}">Read the source on GitHub</a></p>
      <p class="terms">Free and MIT licensed for Node.js 24 or newer, with zero runtime dependencies and the tables in a SQLite database you open.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-art frame">
      <div class="scope"><picture><source media="(min-width: 52rem)" srcset="assets/images/hero-720.webp" width="720" height="540"><img src="assets/images/hero-480.webp" width="480" height="360" alt="A ghost paw drawn in cyan light pressing a glowing hexagonal exclamation mark, violet sparks around it." fetchpriority="high"></picture><span class="scan" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
      <p class="readout" aria-label="Zero runtime dependencies"><span class="big">0</span><span>runtime dependencies</span></p>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="board" class="board-sec" aria-labelledby="board-title">
    <h2 id="board-title">Three quests from the README</h2>
    <p class="intro">Try to finish one with the outcome left blank.</p>
    <p class="intro">This is the Vendor Renewal example from the README, replayed in your browser from a real run: we made the same calls against questlog 0.6.2 on 2026-10-24 with a fixed clock, and every error and every list you see here is what came back, so press Start, leave the outcome empty, press Finish, try to start #3 the way an agent would, then finish #1 for real and watch #3, and jump a week to see the due date go overdue. The live demo runs the library itself.</p>
    <div class="toolbar">
      <p class="today" id="today">Today: Sat 24 Oct</p>
      <button type="button" class="button ghost" id="jump" aria-pressed="false">Jump 7 days</button>
      <button type="button" class="button ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="board">
      <div class="quest" id="q1" data-id="1">
        <p class="q-head"><span class="marker">!</span> <span class="q-label">available</span> <span class="q-id">#1</span></p>
        <h3>Collect redlines</h3>
        <p class="objective">Obtain the latest legal markup.</p>
        <p class="outcome" hidden></p>
        <div class="q-actions">
          <button type="button" class="act start">Start</button>
          <div class="finish" hidden>
            <label for="out-1">Outcome</label>
            <div class="finish-row"><input id="out-1" autocomplete="off" placeholder="What got done?"><button type="button" class="act do-finish">Finish</button></div>
            <p class="refusal" role="status"></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quest" id="q2" data-id="2">
        <p class="q-head"><span class="marker">!</span> <span class="q-label">available</span> <span class="q-id">#2</span></p>
        <h3>Review pricing delta</h3>
        <p class="objective">Compare current vs. proposed cost.</p>
        <p class="outcome" hidden></p>
        <div class="q-actions">
          <button type="button" class="act start">Start</button>
          <div class="finish" hidden>
            <label for="out-2">Outcome</label>
            <div class="finish-row"><input id="out-2" autocomplete="off" placeholder="What got done?"><button type="button" class="act do-finish">Finish</button></div>
            <p class="refusal" role="status"></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quest blocked" id="q3" data-id="3">
        <p class="q-head"><span class="marker">?</span> <span class="q-label">incomplete</span> <span class="q-id">#3</span></p>
        <h3>Obtain finance approval</h3>
        <p class="objective">Sign-off on the new terms. Due Thu 29 Oct.</p>
        <p class="q-stamps"><span class="qstamp block">blocked by #1</span><span class="qstamp due" hidden>overdue</span></p>
        <p class="outcome" hidden></p>
        <div class="q-actions">
          <button type="button" class="act start" hidden>Start</button>
          <button type="button" class="act ask">Start with run_quest</button>
          <p class="refusal tool-refusal" role="status"></p>
          <div class="finish" hidden>
            <label for="out-3">Outcome</label>
            <div class="finish-row"><input id="out-3" autocomplete="off" placeholder="What got done?"><button type="button" class="act do-finish">Finish</button></div>
            <p class="refusal" role="status"></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="calls">
      <p class="calls-label">What your code sees</p>
      <pre><code id="call-log">read.listAvailableQuests(db);
// [2, 1]
read.listBlockedQuests(db);
// [3]
read.listDueSoonQuests(db, 7 * DAY);
// [3]</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="note">A done quest stays done, and a second <code>finishQuest</code> throws "Resolved quests cannot be resolved again."</p>
    <p class="note">Since 0.6.0 blocked holds where your agent acts. The <code>run_quest</code> tool, which the MCP server and the CLI also call, refuses to start #3 with <code>invalid_state</code> and names the open blocker. With <code>force: true</code> it starts the quest anyway and returns the warning "Forced start with unmet prerequisites: Collect redlines."</p>
    <p class="note">The library's own <code>startQuest</code> does not check unlocks, so your code can still start #3 directly. That is on purpose.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="todo" aria-labelledby="todo-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
    <h2 id="todo-title">Where your <code>TODO.md</code> headings go</h2>
    <img class="graph" src="assets/images/art-640.webp" width="640" height="360" alt="Hexagon nodes joined by lines of light: two lit cyan, one locked in violet, the rest faint." loading="lazy">
    </div>
    <div class="todo-grid">
      <pre class="plain"><code>## Todo
- Collect redlines
- Obtain finance approval (after redlines)

## Doing
- Review pricing delta

## Done
- Sent the renewal notice</code></pre>
      <dl class="form">
        <div><dt>Todo</dt><dd>Open quests. The ones nothing waits on carry "!" and show up in <code>listAvailableQuests</code>.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>(after …)</dt><dd>An unlock. The quest sits in <code>listBlockedQuests</code> until its prerequisite finishes with success.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Doing</dt><dd><code>startQuest</code> sets a start time. The marker turns to "?".</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Done</dt><dd><code>finishQuest</code> with an outcome string. <code>abandonQuest</code> records a failure, also with a reason.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>The note in the margin</dt><dd>A rumor. <code>captureRumor</code> holds it until you know what the work is, then <code>settleRumor</code> turns it into a questline and quests.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <p class="intro">None of these states is stored.</p>
    <p class="intro">questlog works them out from the timestamps and the unlocks every time you read. A list cannot go stale, because there is no list.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="time" aria-labelledby="time-title">
    <h2 id="time-title">Deadlines, appointments, repeats</h2>
    <p class="intro">Same table, same quest, and the fields decide what it is.</p>
    <dl class="form">
      <div><dt>A deadline</dt><dd>A quest with <code>dueAt</code>. It moves from due soon to overdue without anyone touching it.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>An appointment</dt><dd>A quest with <code>scheduledStartAt</code> and <code>scheduledEndAt</code>. Missed windows have their own list.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Not before</dt><dd><code>notBeforeAt</code> keeps a quest off the available list until that date.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Every Monday</dt><dd>A repeatable quest with a standard RRULE string spawns a fresh quest each time it comes due.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="worry" aria-labelledby="worry-title">
    <h2 id="worry-title">If agent task trackers have burned you</h2>
    <div class="worry-grid">
      <p>Some agent issue trackers run to hundreds of thousands of lines, and people went back to a markdown file, which is fair enough.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>One package, one bundled file, no runtime dependencies. The numbers are below.</li>
        <li>An outcome is text. It records what the agent claims; it does not run your tests.</li>
        <li>No scheduler and no hosted service. Your code or your agent harness decides when to read.</li>
        <li>Twelve tools with JSON Schemas, served over MCP stdio by <code>npx -y @ghostpaw/questlog mcp</code> or called from your own harness.</li>
        <li>Node.js 24 or newer, because it uses the built-in <code>node:sqlite</code>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="numbers" aria-labelledby="numbers-title">
    <h2 id="numbers-title">What it costs to add</h2>
    <dl class="ledger wide">
      <div><dt>Runtime dependencies</dt><dd>0</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Node.js</dt><dd>24 or newer (node:sqlite)</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Size of dist/index.js, gzip</dt><dd>42.1 KB</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Import time</dt><dd>about 3.7 ms</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Tests</dt><dd>352 passing</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Line coverage</dt><dd>96.0%</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Agent tools</dt><dd>12</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="note">Measured 2026-10-24 on the maintainer's machine with Node.js 24.14.0 against questlog 0.6.1: size of the published dist/index.js at gzip -9, median of 11 cold imports, tests and coverage from the v0.6.1 tag. Import time re-measured on 0.6.2 at low machine load. 0.6.2 only changes the version string and homepage, so size and tests carry over.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="binaries" class="binaries" aria-labelledby="binaries-title">
    <h2 id="binaries-title">Install the release binary</h2>
    <p class="intro">The default way to run <code>ghostpaw-questlog</code>: one executable per platform with Node.js inside, with the same commands and the same MCP server as the npm package. Each line downloads the latest release, checks it against the release&#39;s SHA256SUMS and puts the binary on the PATH (<code>~/.local/bin</code>; the Windows script adds its folder to the user PATH). The lines never edit <code>~/.profile</code>: <code>export PATH</code> lasts for the current shell only. Pin a release with <code>--version &lt;x.y.z&gt;</code>; set <code>GHOSTPAW_NO_MODIFY_PATH=1</code> to keep the Windows script from changing the user PATH.</p>
    <div class="bin-cmds">
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-linux-x64-label">linux-x64</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-linux-x64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-linux-x64-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/questlog/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target linux-x64 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-linux-x64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-linux-arm64-label">linux-arm64</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-linux-arm64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-linux-arm64-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/questlog/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target linux-arm64 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-linux-arm64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-darwin-arm64-label">darwin-arm64</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-darwin-arm64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-darwin-arm64-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/questlog/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target darwin-arm64 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-darwin-arm64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-darwin-x64-label">darwin-x64</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-darwin-x64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-darwin-x64-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/questlog/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target darwin-x64 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-darwin-x64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-windows-x64-label">windows-x64 (PowerShell)</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-windows-x64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-windows-x64-label" spellcheck="false">irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/questlog/main/install.ps1 | iex</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-windows-x64">Copy</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Other release installers</h3>
    <div class="bin-cmds">
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-mise-label">mise</p>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="bin-mise" readonly value="mise use -g github:GhostPawJS/questlog" aria-labelledby="bin-mise-label" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-mise">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-ubi-label">ubi</p>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="bin-ubi" readonly value="ubi --project GhostPawJS/questlog --exe ghostpaw-questlog --in ~/.local/bin" aria-labelledby="bin-ubi-label" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-ubi">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-eget-label">eget</p>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="bin-eget" readonly value="eget GhostPawJS/questlog" aria-labelledby="bin-eget-label" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-eget">Copy</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <h3>npx / npm (for npm-based environments)</h3>
    <div class="bin-cmds">
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-npx-label">npx, with Node.js 24 or newer</p>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="bin-npx" readonly value="npx -y @ghostpaw/questlog --help" aria-labelledby="bin-npx-label" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-npx">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-npm-label">Global npm install</p>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="bin-npm" readonly value="npm install -g @ghostpaw/questlog" aria-labelledby="bin-npm-label" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-npm">Copy</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Library (for harnesses embedding it in code)</h3>
    <div class="bin-cmds">
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-lib-label">Add it to a Node.js 24+ project</p>
        <div class="cmd"><input id="bin-lib" readonly value="npm install @ghostpaw/questlog" aria-labelledby="bin-lib-label" spellcheck="false"><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-lib">Copy</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <dl class="ledger wide">
      <div><dt>linux-x64</dt><dd>41.7 MB tar.gz</dd></div>
      <div><dt>linux-arm64</dt><dd>41.2 MB tar.gz</dd></div>
      <div><dt>darwin-arm64</dt><dd>44.8 MB tar.gz</dd></div>
      <div><dt>darwin-x64</dt><dd>46.4 MB tar.gz</dd></div>
      <div><dt>windows-x64</dt><dd>38.4 MB zip</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="note">Archive sizes of the v0.9.1 release assets. Linux builds need glibc 2.28 or newer; on Alpine, use npx.</p>
    <ul class="bin-trust">
      <li>install.sh and install.ps1 check each archive against SHA256SUMS and stop on a mismatch.</li>
      <li>Each archive and SHA256SUMS carry a GitHub build attestation. Check one with <code>gh attestation verify &lt;archive&gt; -R GhostPawJS/questlog</code>.</li>
      <li>The binaries are not code signed. macOS builds carry an ad-hoc signature, so a browser download needs <code>xattr -d com.apple.quarantine ghostpaw-questlog</code>. Windows may show a SmartScreen warning for a browser download.</li>
    </ul>
    <figure class="shot">
      <a href="{{.urls.cliShot}}"><img src="assets/images/cli-1600.webp" srcset="assets/images/cli-800.webp 800w, assets/images/cli-1600.webp 1600w" sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 72rem, 100vw" width="1600" height="900" decoding="async" alt="Terminal session with questlog 0.9.1: --version prints 0.9.1, three add calls create quests 1 to 3 with tags and due dates, list shows all three, search screenshot finds quest 2, done 2 records the outcome PNG and GIF committed to docs/assets, and show 2 prints every field with state done." loading="lazy"></a>
      <figcaption>A session with the 0.9.1 linux-x64 binary against a fresh database. Open the image for full size.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="links"><a class="more" href="{{.urls.release}}">Release v0.9.1</a><a href="{{.urls.readmeInstall}}">Install notes in the README</a><a href="{{.urls.attest}}">gh attestation verify</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <h2 id="start-title">Start from the README</h2>
    <pre><code>import { DatabaseSync } from 'node:sqlite';
import { initQuestlogTables, read, write } from '@ghostpaw/questlog';

const db = new DatabaseSync(':memory:');
initQuestlogTables(db);

const rumor = write.captureRumor(db, {
  title: 'Legal says the vendor terms changed',
  details: 'Need to understand pricing delta and termination clause.',
});

write.settleRumor(db, rumor.id, {
  settledAt: Date.now(),
  questline: {
    title: 'Vendor Renewal',
    description: 'Commercial, legal, and approval work.',
  },
  quests: [
    { title: 'Collect redlines', objective: 'Obtain the latest legal markup.' },
    { title: 'Review pricing delta', objective: 'Compare current vs. proposed cost.' },
  ],
});

const available = read.listAvailableQuests(db);
const dueSoon = read.listDueSoonQuests(db, 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);</code></pre>
    <p>Agents get twelve tools, among them <code>review_questlog</code>, <code>capture_rumor</code>, <code>shape_work</code>, <code>run_quest</code> and <code>reward_work</code>, and each one returns success, no_op, needs_clarification or error with a hint for the next step.</p>
    <p class="links"><a class="more" href="{{.urls.readme}}">Read the README</a><a href="{{.urls.demo}}">Open the live demo</a><a href="{{.urls.npm}}">questlog on npm</a></p>
    <nav class="docs-map" aria-labelledby="docs-map-title">
      <h3 id="docs-map-title">{{.data.docs.heading}}</h3>
      <ul>
        {{range .data.docs.pages}}<li><a href="{{index $.urls .key}}">{{.label}}</a><span>{{.note}}</span></li>{{end}}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </section>
</main>
